During upgrade, the new manifest’s dependencies are recorded but never validated (missing deps / incompatible versions). This can leave the registry in an inconsistent state after a “successful” upgrade. Consider re-running the same dependency validation logic as `install()` (including version constraint checks) before committing the upgraded record.
```suggestion
    // 4. Register new namespaces and validate dependencies before updating record
    this.namespaceResolver.register(packageId, newNamespaces);
    const deps = (newManifest as any).dependencies as Record<string, string> | undefined;

    // 5. Validate that all declared dependencies are installed and version-compatible
    if (deps && Object.keys(deps).length > 0) {
      const missingDeps: string[] = [];
      const incompatibleDeps: { depId: string; required: string; actual: string }[] = [];

      for (const [depId, versionRange] of Object.entries(deps)) {
        const installedDep = this.packages.get(depId);
        if (!installedDep) {
          missingDeps.push(depId);
          continue;
        }

        try {
          const installedSemver = SemanticVersionManager.parse(installedDep.version);
          if (!SemanticVersionManager.satisfies(installedSemver, versionRange)) {
            incompatibleDeps.push({
              depId,
              required: versionRange,
              actual: installedDep.version,
            });
          }
        } catch {
          // Treat parse errors as incompatibilities to avoid accepting invalid versions
          incompatibleDeps.push({
            depId,
            required: versionRange,
            actual: installedDep.version,
          });
        }
      }

      if (missingDeps.length > 0 || incompatibleDeps.length > 0) {
        // Roll back namespace registration on dependency validation failure
        this.namespaceResolver.unregister(packageId);
        this.namespaceResolver.register(packageId, existing.namespaces);

        const problems: string[] = [];
        if (missingDeps.length > 0) {
          problems.push(`missing: ${missingDeps.join(', ')}`);
        }
        if (incompatibleDeps.length > 0) {
          const details = incompatibleDeps
            .map(d => `${d.depId} (required ${d.required}, installed ${d.actual})`)
            .join('; ');
          problems.push(`incompatible versions: ${details}`);
        }

        return {
          success: false,
          packageId,
          fromVersion: existing.version,
          toVersion: newVersion,
          snapshot,
          errorMessage: `Dependency validation failed for new version: ${problems.join(' | ')}`,
        };
      }
    }

    // 6. All checks passed, persist upgraded record
```

`NamespaceResolver.register` overwrites an existing namespace entry even when it is owned by a different package (it only logs a warning). This defeats collision prevention: a later registration can silently steal ownership and make `checkAvailability` results unreliable. Consider refusing to overwrite (throw/return conflicts) when `existing.packageId !== packageId`, and keep registration as an invariant enforced by the caller.
```suggestion
          const message = `Namespace collision for "${ns}" between packages "${existing.packageId}" (existing) and "${packageId}" (incoming)`;
          this.logger.error('Namespace registration conflict', {
            namespace: ns,
            existing: existing.packageId,
            incoming: packageId,
            message,
          });
          throw new Error(message);
```

`PluginPublish` posts JSON metadata to `/packages/upload`, but the API contract expects `multipart/form-data` with both `{ artifact: <metadata>, file: <binary> }` (see `UploadArtifactRequestSchema`). As written, a conforming marketplace service will reject this request and the actual artifact bytes are never uploaded. Switch to multipart upload and include the artifact file contents alongside the metadata.
```suggestion
      // Perform HTTP upload as multipart/form-data:
      // - "artifact": JSON metadata
      // - "file": binary artifact contents
      const formData = new FormData();

      // Attach metadata as JSON
      const artifactJson = JSON.stringify(uploadPayload);
      if (typeof Blob !== 'undefined') {
        formData.append('artifact', new Blob([artifactJson], { type: 'application/json' }));
      } else {
        formData.append('artifact', artifactJson);
      }

      // Attach binary artifact file
      const artifactFileName = path.basename(artifactPath);
      if (typeof Blob !== 'undefined') {
        formData.append('file', new Blob([artifactBuffer]), artifactFileName);
      } else {
        // Fallback: rely on FormData accepting Buffer/Uint8Array in this runtime
        formData.append('file', artifactBuffer as any, artifactFileName);
      }

      const response = await fetch(uploadUrl, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Authorization': `Bearer ${flags.token}`,
        },
        body: formData,
```

Dependency handling during install only checks that dependency package IDs exist; it doesn’t validate version constraints (e.g. `^1.0.0`) and doesn’t use `DependencyResolver` for conflict detection/topological ordering. This can allow installs that violate declared constraints. Consider using `DependencyResolver.detectConflicts`/`findBestVersion` (or at least `SemanticVersionManager.satisfies`) to enforce dependency ranges.
```suggestion

    const missingDeps: string[] = [];
    const incompatibleDeps: { packageId: string; required: string; installed: string }[] = [];

    for (const depId of depNames) {
      const installedDep = this.packages.get(depId);
      if (!installedDep) {
        missingDeps.push(depId);
        continue;
      }

      const requiredRange = deps?.[depId];
      if (requiredRange) {
        const installedSemver = SemanticVersionManager.parse(installedDep.version);
        if (!SemanticVersionManager.satisfies(installedSemver, requiredRange)) {
          incompatibleDeps.push({
            packageId: depId,
            required: requiredRange,
            installed: installedDep.version,
          });
        }
      }
    }

    if (missingDeps.length > 0 || incompatibleDeps.length > 0) {
      const messages: string[] = [];
      if (missingDeps.length > 0) {
        messages.push(`missing: ${missingDeps.join(', ')}`);
      }
      if (incompatibleDeps.length > 0) {
        const details = incompatibleDeps
          .map(d => `${d.packageId} (required ${d.required}, installed ${d.installed})`)
          .join('; ');
        messages.push(`version conflicts: ${details}`);
      }

      return {
        success: false,
        packageId,
        version,
        installedDependencies: [],
        namespaceConflicts: [],
        errorMessage: `Unmet dependencies: ${messages.join(' | ')}`,
